+Implementation note
+-------------------
+A single fused kernel computes both the loss and the gradient. Each program
+handles one row: a first streaming pass performs an online softmax (running
+max, running sum of exponentials, sum of logits, target logit — O(1) state per
+row), and a second pass recomputes the probabilities block-by-block and writes
+the gradient in place into the ``logits`` buffer. The only extra device memory
+is an ``(N,)`` float32 buffer of per-row losses; no full-size ``(N, V)``
+intermediate is ever materialized.
